								<span
									class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[13px] font-semibold text-[#afe3d0] tabular-nums dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]"
								>
									1
								</span>
								<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink">
									Cut Filler Phrases &amp; Redundancies
								</h3>
							</div>
							<p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-body">
								Replace wordy phrases like <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"due to the fact that"</strong> with <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"because"</strong>, <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"in order to"</strong> with <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"to"</strong>, and <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"at this point in time"</strong> with <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"now"</strong>. Prune unnecessary padding to immediately recover 5–10% of your total word limit.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Card 2 -->
					<div
						class="flex flex-col justify-between rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-elevated p-6 transition-all hover:border-[#0f2e26]/30 dark:hover:border-[#afe3d0]/30"
					>
						<div>
							<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
								<span
									class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[13px] font-semibold text-[#afe3d0] tabular-nums dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]"
								>
									2
								</span>
								<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink">
									Convert Passive Voice to Active Voice
								</h3>
							</div>
							<p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-body">
								Change <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"The experiment was conducted by the researchers"</strong> (8 words) to <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"The researchers conducted the experiment"</strong> (5 words) to trim ~20–30% wordiness. Active voice tightens sentence momentum and strengthens academic rigor.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Card 3 -->
					<div
						class="flex flex-col justify-between rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-elevated p-6 transition-all hover:border-[#0f2e26]/30 dark:hover:border-[#afe3d0]/30"
					>
						<div>
							<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
								<span
									class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[13px] font-semibold text-[#afe3d0] tabular-nums dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]"
								>
									3
								</span>
								<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink">
									Trim Weak Adverbs &amp; Qualifiers
								</h3>
							</div>
							<p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-body">
								Remove <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"very"</strong>, <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"really"</strong>, <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"basically"</strong>, and <strong class="font-medium text-ink">"actually"</strong> when the verb or adjective already carries the meaning. Strong, specific verbs (e.g., "demolished" instead of "completely destroyed") naturally lower word counts.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Card 4 -->
					<div
						class="flex flex-col justify-between rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-elevated p-6 transition-all hover:border-[#0f2e26]/30 dark:hover:border-[#afe3d0]/30"
					>
						<div>
							<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
								<span
									class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[13px] font-semibold text-[#afe3d0] tabular-nums dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]"
								>
									4
								</span>
								<h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink">
									Tighten Introductions &amp; Repetitive Transitions
								</h3>
							</div>
							<p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-body">
								Keep essay openings crisp (10–12% of total word count) and merge overlapping summary sentences. Avoid prolonged throat-clearing before your thesis statement, and delete redundant connective phrases between paragraphs.
							</p>
